<h2>Course notes</h2>
<p>Every module in the outline above links to its full lecture notes: the ideas in plain language, every line of code
  with its real output, figures, and exercises. The notes follow Daniel Bourke's free book
  <a href="https://www.learnpytorch.io/" rel="noopener">Learn PyTorch for Deep Learning</a> chapter for chapter, so the
  book gives you a second explanation of everything here.</p>
<p><a class="link-quiet" href="{{ '/teaching/aibasic/00-pytorch-fundamentals/' | relative_url }}">Start with module 00, PyTorch fundamentals →</a></p>

<h2>How the course runs</h2>
<p>Classes are hands-on. We work through each module live in Colab, and you type the code as we go — reading code is
  no substitute for writing it. The exercises at the end of each module are the best practice for the assignments and
  the midterm.</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Attendance (10%)</strong> — short pop quizzes at random points in the term.</li>
  <li><strong>Programming assignments (30%)</strong> — two assignments, posted on
    <a href="https://ublearns.buffalo.edu/d2l/login" rel="noopener">UBlearns</a>.</li>
  <li><strong>Midterm exam (30%)</strong> — in week 7, covering weeks 1–5.</li>
  <li><strong>Group project (30%)</strong> — teams carry a problem of their choosing through the whole workflow of the
    course, from data to a deployed model, and present it in the final weeks. Start early, and ask questions whenever
    you have them.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Getting set up</h2>
<p>You need a Google account and a web browser — nothing to install. All code runs in
  <a href="https://colab.research.google.com/" rel="noopener">Google Colab</a>, which provides Python, PyTorch, and a free
  GPU. Module 00 walks through the first notebook step by step.</p>

<h3>Warm-up courses (optional bonus)</h3>
<p>If you have never programmed before, these free freeCodeCamp courses are a gentle way in, and a good use of a few
  weekends early in the term:</p>
<ul>
  <li><a href="https://www.freecodecamp.org/learn/scientific-computing-with-python/" rel="noopener">Scientific Computing with Python</a></li>
  <li><a href="https://www.freecodecamp.org/learn/data-analysis-with-python/" rel="noopener">Data Analysis with Python</a></li>
  <li><a href="https://www.freecodecamp.org/learn/college-algebra-with-python/" rel="noopener">College Algebra with Python</a></li>
</ul>
<p>Complete them and attach the certificates to your final project report for a 15-point bonus.</p>
